#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119631 :question/id #uuid "0a0ea798-5125-5d0e-a755-96bf9af5f543" :question/math-academy-id "e-4823" :question/problem "Find the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ if $\\,\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ and\n$$\n\\mathbf{b_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}3 \\\\ - 4 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}, \n\t\\qquad \n\t\\mathbf{b_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]},\n\t\\qquad\n\t[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 1 \\\\ 3\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,\\mathcal{B}.$ Since we are told that $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 1 \\\\ 3\\end{array} \\right]},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\underbrace{(-1)}_{{x}_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\underbrace{(\\,3\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119632 :question/id #uuid "6c7237cd-c655-575f-83ac-7a0891c336b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4824" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{b_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{b_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{x}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 5 \\\\ - 11 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n$$\nM =\t \\left[{\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & - 5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & - 11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & - 8\\end{array}}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ -4{x}_{2} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left( -1 \\right)  = -5\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad\nx_1 = -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 2 \\\\ - 1\\end{array} \\right]}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119633 :question/id #uuid "90f07e38-405a-5f79-8501-0b4dfb8fa4c8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4825" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{b_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]}, \\quad\n\t\\mathbf{b_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}3 \\\\ - 9 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}, \\quad\n\t\\mathbf{b_3}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ - 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]}, \\quad\n\t\\mathbf{x}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=7 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3} &=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}4 \\\\ - 1 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119674 :question/id #uuid "a79126f2-e26c-5929-93d8-825d85b9a438" :question/math-academy-id "e-6282" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{b_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{b_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{x}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ - 5\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{ {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ - 5\\end{array} \\right]}}_{\\mathbf{x}} = \\underbrace{(\\,-5\\,)}_{x_1} \\cdot \\underbrace{ {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]}}_{\\mathbf{b}_1} + \\underbrace{(\\:2\\:)}_{x_2} \\cdot \\underbrace{ {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}}_{\\mathbf{b}_2}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 5 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028867b0-8cf6-524a-93e6-8e63fa02e23d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317580} {:answer/id #uuid "2f329de5-7c1a-5fad-b2d2-f7cc8384731d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317709} {:answer/id #uuid "5f5bbc70-a2a7-5d4f-9c69-50122cef639d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317888} {:answer/id #uuid "844d0795-32e6-5eb9-9815-e5906f5fb3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318014} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c361cd-49f5-527f-91c1-eb17cbe67bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "028867b0-8cf6-524a-93e6-8e63fa02e23d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317580} :answer-field/id #uuid "add90972-43b4-50ff-b652-f7e992bc2ad7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f17a8e42-194f-52ed-9136-123dd348b4bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-34617" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{2} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-2)+2=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120357 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ade3deb-0ace-50bf-b347-4bfcae190b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∉ Span{b_{1}, b_{2}, b_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118257} {:answer/id #uuid "a7171ecf-ef5e-5114-8ce9-be792596a33b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118258} {:answer/id #uuid "1f823a42-0358-51e6-b50b-0cf9106108f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118259} {:answer/id #uuid "3284a369-5a47-5bff-a487-8bbadb8765d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118260} {:answer/id #uuid "5c31a331-ffe6-5e82-8dbe-323ad3e29a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118261}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c79da9b6-1615-5606-9505-7a69edc00bff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "53146aef-5e01-515d-a2c7-6125691cccf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34762" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}, b_{3}}$, where\n$$\n\\displaystyle b_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}, b_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, b_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\nIf $[x]_{B} = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19420cda-b431-5a47-899b-f28a5a79a06e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317647} {:answer/id #uuid "4894ab4c-1533-51ce-99f5-6fe4ab34c2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317806} {:answer/id #uuid "a99ae0f6-7d7b-5bcf-bdc9-3cee8244b3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318142} {:answer/id #uuid "e58ca5c8-718c-5e6d-b05d-4eeffbd0538a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318331} {:answer/id #uuid "c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430722} :answer-field/id #uuid "e31b6e05-fbe4-51d6-9c76-36484db39779" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "127eef35-0ba2-54bf-857c-c0aaa600443a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34764" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ -{x}_{3} &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere the fourth equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2513b831-2bda-5222-a175-9dbc2cbe0fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-21 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430711} {:answer/id #uuid "29376ce5-1709-5e3d-9b46-93794cef8b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430712} {:answer/id #uuid "54390e6e-dcb1-5dd3-95c7-15b36777dc0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430714} {:answer/id #uuid "916a198b-9533-5031-bb1d-8a1a6d13d6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430719} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430723} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5940cf3-d0a0-564c-9b31-70b2bd92b22b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fd151813-8e78-53b9-b9c5-57f0cca18b33" :question/math-academy-id "q-35232" :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\underbrace{(\\,-3\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\underbrace{(\\,5\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}25 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa86c844-6610-527e-88a2-af6e5bd7c06b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∉ Span{b_{1}, b_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118395} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d663dd-58a4-520b-8a52-f0e4e92796b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118396} {:answer/id #uuid "5a0769e5-3e36-5274-b047-dd8f9c324e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118397} {:answer/id #uuid "5d37b2b7-79a1-5071-89eb-69ff6bc40d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118398} {:answer/id #uuid "660740bc-ad82-5ba0-94ac-c929475067c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118399}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d8f3ac9d-6dc0-50b8-97c8-53dc4fcfba3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118394}] 