d8a390-94af-51c7-aa98-818f4e35ea3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319718} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9c2874-3632-5825-955d-71bf02cc70ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b9c2874-3632-5825-955d-71bf02cc70ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319762} :answer-field/id #uuid "f02f8758-8a19-581b-83ba-bb98079edf99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b9b88237-ebd3-525d-97e2-e2d2efea1ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-35215" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 6 & 10 & -2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 10 & -2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ 5{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ 0 &=0,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the fourth equation, we get a true statement. Then, from the second and third equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1$ and  ${x}_{3}=2$ respectively. Substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}+5(1)=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e70132-b4c9-52d8-a99a-a454c18aea30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342570} {:answer/id #uuid "57870f92-6f97-5e07-99ce-3444e70735a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342968} {:answer/id #uuid "5b4f5e5b-d060-5823-a3f2-e785ef7bf05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343001} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0ffb85-7797-55b4-8740-01d2092d531a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343753} {:answer/id #