n$$\nx=4\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-3)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\,\\,-3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "081a40c5-551f-580d-b01c-1d60d32cb060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342306} {:answer/id #uuid "0d73c50f-626b-5a8e-a458-314c34867174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342352} {:answer/id #uuid "1f356320-8189-5405-b803-d0029934a836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342496} {:answer/id #uuid "d3020996-e213-5e09-92b5-f8f81fe30866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344088} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b57cbb-63bc-5327-8a0a-50b2fe957a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3020996-e213-5e09-92b5-f8f81fe30866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344088} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe5461c8-51c8-5591-bfc3-b3c528e3db44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "32d360b2-b07c-58ea-8316-13ed526cce1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75978" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}=\\underbrace{(\\,-8\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(\\,4\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{2}}+\\underbrace{(\\,2\\,)}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=-8\\cdot {b}_{1}+4\\cdot {b}_{2}+2\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38af80af-d49d-54b5-aaac-e804ec8c572f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342704} {:answer/id #uuid "599365f9-b07b-5a51-90c6-591c6ef0676c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342989} {:answer/id #uuid "6f11f370-7154-5e9c-a4e9-b57216fdc44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343195} {:answer/id #uuid "7661a5d2-790d-560a-bb3e-426238e8cf3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343264} {:answer/id #uuid "891b0ab7-d32f-5dea-abb7-0b327f3d717c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "599365f9-b07b-5a51-90c6-591c6ef0676c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342989} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae94580-b08e-514f-af33-6d3e14d4f24e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4061dc6a-87c8-53d1-aa6a-18325afc93ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-75984" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}=\\underbrace{(\\,-2\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(\\,-1\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{2}}+\\underbrace{(\\,5\\,)}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=-2\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-1)\\cdot {b}_{2}+5\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{3}=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f2ff65-44fc-5ef9-91c5-f15a1dcb4482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342558} {:answer/id #uuid "58cfce89-35bf-5090-bd09-7a131045a8f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342984} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1bfdd8-5fa9-56ce-9f81-0cfeccd976c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343327} {:answer/id #uuid "987ef422-3991-5a26-a987-a7bbdaa181ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343578} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c2e89a-83ba-550e-972d-3d894352b88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58cfce89-35bf-5090-bd09-7a131045a8f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342984} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1ba166-fcf8-5656-a4b3-d70644c35317" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4d18b23f-7f2c-58d6-9c7b-1f111a7cab73" :question/math-academy-id "q-75989" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 0 &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere the third equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that $x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "219502e3-af31-5611-9ead-5045a9c248d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342516} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf985a4-355e-5261-ad9f-710c6c8bed01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342733} {:answer/id #uuid "58c1eed9-7736-5df0-b819-e18f099e18a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342982} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5abdda-188a-520d-bbdf-83d23c0b19b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344313} {:answer/id #uuid "5de78ea6-b293-58dc-961e-a74b7da29c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec5abdda-188a-520d-bbdf-83d23c0b19b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344313} :answer-field/id #uuid "309b2ee3-ef9f-541d-ba25-643af6f67641" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b9b1c708-0429-5e44-9bc9-a554cb44ed9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76056" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 7 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 25 & -25\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ 25{x}_{3} &=-25.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)-(-1)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a2b0007-b1ff-5146-ba23-84221b2f5975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386601} {:answer/id #uuid "669e4748-3a82-5a26-8c10-892abe146140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386602} {:answer/id #uuid "269a80ec-f612-5e73-a5e0-a54472488f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386603} {:answer/id #uuid "75cc7f40-a26d-597e-b210-e69eaecff962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386604} {:answer/id #uuid "3fabbf7d-efda-5358-94f9-a35c8f5a7dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a2b0007-b1ff-5146-ba23-84221b2f5975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386601} :answer-field/id #uuid "84c6e32a-b0c7-5909-8bf3-21a7bc429f26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "413cbee8-b598-5cbf-b19b-566a259d8943" :question/math-academy-id "q-112242" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ \n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+5=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c2b8825-d0f3-5cf3-8772-66a5bebe2a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391905} {:answer/id #uuid "2a76e81c-9f5c-58e3-92b5-2eb7e44c3e8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391906} {:answer/id #uuid "61a90cd4-b7c0-5ccc-b6a1-7d72d7048fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391907} {:answer/id #uuid "3b85a6f7-eafc-5b67-9e8d-a43f841a9bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391908} {:answer/id #uuid "aabd78f7-b086-5589-a005-8319378aba32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c2b8825-d0f3-5cf3-8772-66a5bebe2a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391905} :answer-field/id #uuid "be439d06-f9b7-505b-a37e-5f2a910df93d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6262ea2d-1b8c-5ef7-8314-13d0b021a42e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35218" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ -2{x}_{2} &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 2=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1+2=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73075c87-a5af-52f3-b076-c875aaab0c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391912} {:answer/id #uuid "0e580b3b-adfa-5089-8b27-15ec64aa2c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -