ix}+\\underbrace{(\\,5\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}= \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -25\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ab819f-c33e-5cef-9c7d-94cc01a08eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409788} {:answer/id #uuid "67fe8fd6-4155-5cce-93e6-650aa08ca771" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409796} {:answer/id #uuid "8c55afca-aada-59e7-8566-a67479e5ca90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409799} {:answer/id #uuid "bd67ec1c-d0b6-583a-93ea-2320fc866ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409804} {:answer/id #uuid "d730889c-d211-5f79-808d-edb05582ebf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd67ec1c-d0b6-583a-93ea-2320fc866ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409804} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1adc025-e35c-5c7f-b3d2-a22f6c131b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "893314bd-9641-54d7-a9c3-9945a815ea4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-112246" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -16\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-14 \\\\ -2{x}_{2} &=-16.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=8.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(8)=-14\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-6)+8=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2115aac5-da66-5510-8b11-176ba754f81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409789} {:answer/id #uuid "45dbc0e6-16a9-5c62-a183-2dd30e767a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409790} {:answer/id #uuid "60013665-0a5a-5449-9017-6cb6ae7ed2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409792} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad6f309-f775-5604-ba46-fa9609a5688b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409798} {:answer/id #uuid "ba977b58-8add-5c57-ae69-640a36ab4ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60013665-0a5a-5449-9017-6cb6ae7ed2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409792} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe323417-1cf2-5a08-b6a1-9d36f7d769a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d9b245f0-31aa-56fe-aa26-5663dd9e140f" :question/math-academy-id "q-112211" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}=\\underbrace{(\\,-8\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(\\,-7\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=(-8)\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-7)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56a6c136-0c09-5ee6-8667-b8c578a8d106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409791} {:answer/id #uuid "60f7a927-bdd2-5f05-8617-e8e1e2381233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409793} {:answer/id #uuid "71804a18-d46f-54b8-91e7-a3197dfed1f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409797} {:answer/id #uuid "ca4c5e51-eb69-5a8f-82a6-2590266e47b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409805} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb18c3c-3fae-5461-a45e-727641240832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71804a18-d46f-54b8-91e7-a3197dfed1f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409797} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea7b226f-79df-5fde-bf3b-18e9fc4ba990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ebceb075-efc9-5bc0-95d2-77852526cbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-112251" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -38 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -38 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{12}{19}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -19{x}_{2} &=-38.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-5(2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10+2=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0470cd3b-2bcb-575e-9def-d43004406207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409787} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e208c3-ba1a-51ec-b367-c2784fabe06c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409800} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ba42a7-b00b-5980-9f89-48160c1eb49e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409801} {:answer/id #uuid "d13c159c-f442-5933-a821-d94880c3ba32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409806} {:answer/id #uuid "eec553dd-6fd7-5208-9292-850213e9c19b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5ba42a7-b00b-5980-9f89-48160c1eb49e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409801} :answer-field/id #uuid "a79bee7d-12b6-5017-ae13-ca00a861bd24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ec45397c-5ced-5a47-b9a9-86c6aa1d1bf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76073" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ \\,\\,-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ \\,\\,0 &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere the third equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b2da92-80e1-5a61-a19c-e0402c5db36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416936} {:answer/id #uuid "94ec8a9d-591d-59ec-b9c5-a655500ebc04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416937} {:answer/id #uuid "c791cf81-feb5-59a1-bf25-b0be74c138f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416940} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdbeb50-bd46-5e6a-a5d9-d2fa3f1bb293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416942} {:answer/id #uuid "f2716f4b-b756-5daf-b7ff-420d367fb480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b2da92-80e1-5a61-a19c-e0402c5db36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416936} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd25317-6ae7-5ed2-b2f8-06a74441129a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1098aac8-90b3-5ba0-b447-7ead2947d568" :question/math-academy-id "q-35247" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=-8 \\\\ 4{x}_{2} &=20.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}-4(5)=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+5=9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e83f3a8-e73e-5dcd-ac90-e7fbd7a63237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426844} {:answer/id #uuid "1298c82b-5f34-5b3d-9a2e-19a4db3c3122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426845} {:answer/id #uuid "6f2c222c-23e3-58cc-87ec-9f7920cb1f7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426847} {:answer/id #uuid "b92f0488-96a7-580a-9581-5603eab3169c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426851} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9d08f1-fc9e-5876-bc5a-62f5443e92fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1298c82b-5f34-5b3d-9a2e-19a4db3c3122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426845} :answer-field/id #uuid "3659e401-201b-5665-a817-8016820a5661" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "973ba0d1-71e0-5bd1-b707-8f3f23076709" :question/math-academy-id "q-34761" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ 12{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=16 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second  equation yields\n\n$$\n12{x}_{2}+2(2)=16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+4(1)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+1+2=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06febdbc-65f9-5901-99f7-6a7827495ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426843} {:answer/id #uuid "5fac1657-f0bf-58cd-839a-2936f55e9617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426846} {:answer/id #uuid "922920ae-5499-5f5e-8c1f-2a7d78b98e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426848} {:answer/id #uuid "a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426849} {:answer/id #uuid "de386f32-9648-5557-95da-e81b5a893cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426849} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbd70cc-1860-587f-a06b-f6be24d7a7e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310" :question/math-academy-id "q-112247" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 15\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2} &=15.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-4)+(-3)=-7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82bca19e-14cc-56cc-9397-e33111aae553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430716} {:answer/id #uuid "8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430717} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8f1b4f-ea6f-50a7-90b7-28a18c762dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430718} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f552c7-b78f-5465-9564-878cf6243fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430720} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c9c363-73dc-5320-b19f-2ebf3f0d2405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430717} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d8ec2ef-2c05-5932-bd6d-c9b93200f648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7fd80750-80bf-5e1d-b08d-abec51a32d9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112213" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 40\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ -10{x}_{2} &=40.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-4)=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce43d07-7d46-5c98-b744-3a88ad395201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430713} {:answer/id #uuid "b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430721} {:answer/id #uuid "d52b898d-8b0d-5322-b32b-d790188a0c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430724} {:answer/id #uuid "e60504c0-156d-5be5-b8b0-a6c50751ba29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-23 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430726} {:answer/id #uuid "f9aaf9bb-e91f-5b1b-81ad-71ec2b8c9df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430721} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e865a75-dfdd-5a58-b928-640a4073b739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8a5b5cd1-19ba-524a-960c-18e8a17d885d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112202" :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\underbrace{(\\,3\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\underbrace{(\\,-3\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "066bb7c4-7521-5727-993a-55db17b87282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454919} {:answer/id #uuid "49378edd-134f-5712-a720-7f1c131c32c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455026} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f74b12-935c-5e33-a5e5-220baef222b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455198} {:answer/id #uuid "b4852b6d-9a78-5d08-bc44-0fc169587a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455217} {:answer/id #uuid "f9fc417c-d758-5208-baf3-43da35bca066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9fc417c-d758-5208-baf3-43da35bca066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455333} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa3925e-da8c-56e5-b9b6-c047f1edb4c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3d89aeef-7acc-5575-9764-44e144045f82" :question/math-academy-id "q-75998" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=-7 \\\\ -3{x}_{3} &=-6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}-2(2)=-7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(3)+2=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSo, we have ${x}_{1}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2679ade7-de7e-5ff4-88c8-94968abbecd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454962} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4e66c0-8e5c-5dff-8789-8ac0302fb04b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454974} {:answer/id #uuid "58225722-5487-53b4-b242-37a168921893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455056} {:answer/id #uuid "a19f8251-ccaa-52d8-8b83-bba63f64cb63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455191} {:answer/id #uuid "f7cbfdfe-250f-5f75-93f6-f1ca311bd2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2679ade7-de7e-5ff4-88c8-94968abbecd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454962} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c6024f5-9069-597b-a291-cd59361ac136" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e3764343-10e9-5a7d-b034-e095faf7f51c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76054" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -27\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=15 \\\\ -9{x}_{3} &=-27.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+3(3)=15\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=3$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3+3=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+3+3=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7700fc74-62d9-5c43-a14e-3089802b8f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527530} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1c50f8-8c07-5027-b319-7781b3d31cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527631} {:answer/id #uuid "afa06ac1-854a-5acd-a258-9948876f2387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527668} {:answer/id #uuid "d197d8cb-a53e-5fcb-9f95-86830c4ab9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527731} {:answer/id #uuid "e51a43de-aaa3-5ca0-b2ff-dd23d8bf03d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7700fc74-62d9-5c43-a14e-3089802b8f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527530} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bb29f16-8d05-55d0-ab1d-19d482085ecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527857}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7c3f2557-93da-5d6b-97fe-29c0805f0db0" :question/math-academy-id "q-75975" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $$\n\\displaystyle [x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}=\\underbrace{(\\,6\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(\\,-3\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=6\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-3)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186597543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5930987b-fff4-5a39-8a89-9aea0aaab9cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597047} {:answer/id #uuid "8024b10f-f049-5325-8434-544d99072bb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597119} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a54c94-ba11-5018-a042-3123b0f21b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597198} {:answer/id #uuid "d75d57f6-0aaa-5cea-b551-e6aec51ef26e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597297} {:answer/id #uuid "de4ea52d-8ecc-5d27-8c76-1b849848916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de4ea52d-8ecc-5d27-8c76-1b849848916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597310} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f83c79-3fae-5558-aadf-80864447ddaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "10aeda88-9cde-589e-adbd-43cffc4b40f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-76074" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ \\,\\,-2{x}_{3} &=-5 \\\\ \\,\\,0 &=-4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere the fourth equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186597545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b11a14c-3591-53fc-8d00-8d9240f87d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596887} {:answer/id #uuid "65f1991f-77bc-5d36-b18e-491432e9f4d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597076} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4eba49-0429-5bd3-9d6d-e4c7ff5ba70e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597177} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e8fc97-b78f-51a2-8174-73994cb68f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597182} {:answer/id #uuid "af3c24d5-0beb-5796-bbf8-8bf0e7b29bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0e8fc97-b78f-51a2-8174-73994cb68f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597182} :answer-field/id #uuid "3675f345-9e4e-5392-b916-d381cb447096" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1ce15171-670f-5275-8d95-63e5a7ab2738" :question/math-academy-id "q-112292" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 & -18\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 27 & -27\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=10 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3} &=-3 \\\\ 27{x}_{3} &=-27.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the  third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$  Substituting this value into the second equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+7(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(2)-(-1)=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+2+(-1)=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186597560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f36539d-06c4-517b-9f7c-f34fb072cef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596927} {:answer/id #uuid "9c27ba1e-a130-554c-9b9d-4d9c4803b17c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597174} {:answer/id #uuid "c4c6f472-938a-5805-bf21-a16449ce5dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597256} {:answer/id #uuid "f23a72c6-3233-5091-9efc-497d23ab29b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597354} {:answer/id #uuid "f80ce284-6da3-5914-aa39-6676aa9e9f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4c6f472-938a-5805-bf21-a16449ce5dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597256} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbb6c772-eb69-5765-bfd4-56aaf6ecbc0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4ab01065-594d-557c-9a66-63b954ed84d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75985" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,9\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=9\\cdot {b}_{1}+4\\cdot {b}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}=9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186597565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23aa80c8-2a74-5eab-ad22-b6840a50754e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596935} {:answer/id #uuid "41758b06-325c-553d-8e0d-917d2f692acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596997} {:answer/id #uuid "5783218a-f4ca-587e-9f3b-6983a142a861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597043} {:answer/id #uuid "81a6bb19-4f2d-50d0-baca-04d4a588e9e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860