{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186597603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00771a22-a8e2-5ab2-bd5a-17f3d5767dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596866} {:answer/id #uuid "297df4c8-a197-59e3-98bb-0693299bc013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596946} {:answer/id #uuid "6b82b381-a57a-5eb8-aa41-fc37a8b24df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597086} {:answer/id #uuid "8b54520c-ffea-5acf-93ef-2519a62b5f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597140} {:answer/id #uuid "b0625232-ae81-5f02-9993-cb492793ab1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00771a22-a8e2-5ab2-bd5a-17f3d5767dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596866} :answer-field/id #uuid "c658e329-493b-5f45-b738-0d07bd9e7d67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dbfd6a51-7b9e-51a0-805c-69c38508d2a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-112210" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-6\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,7\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=(-5)\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-6)\\cdot {b}_{2}+7\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{3}=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186651578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3593ad9e-a556-5dda-a8be-f609ea0e2071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651133} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8e22a1-4af7-55d4-9830-67479f0fb592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651145} {:answer/id #uuid "b44130e7-98d4-502c-92fe-96dbd6f02a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651309} {:answer/id #uuid "d76a4e0d-64fc-5d40-8bd4-41e74e97f646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651368} {:answer/id #uuid "f5eda25e-0dc6-59ad-9734-30dc4b6bbb4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3593ad9e-a556-5dda-a8be-f609ea0e2071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651133} :answer-field/id #uuid "79581498-6892-596c-88e9-ad157bd1b79c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4ff87d79-64c7-5f42-af26-5d490510ffea" :question/math-academy-id "q-112212" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}=\\underbrace{(\\,-4\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(\\,4\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=(-4)\\cdot {b}_{1}+4\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186651595 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de3d03d-c907-57c9-982e-ebec5479eea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651097} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9b2420-28b7-5d0c-8114-46c9f370c600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651244} {:answer/id #uuid "8723caf8-0fe6-5ce7-bad0-29d84d636091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651256} {:answer/id #uuid "96695986-7974-5e82-b6b3-e5e1b4a333ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651269} {:answer/id #uuid "efb66b01-e7f5-59d3-9183-a68b96a51e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96695986-7974-5e82-b6b3-e5e1b4a333ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651269} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d736fd3-4f26-5afc-a62c-bf6662e99fec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7b404627-3418-5d75-8f08-d3070eca19ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-75990" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{6}{10}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ -10{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 0 &=-3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere the third equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that $x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186651629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9ad8e6-2807-51ae-8166-b2eebb145e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651065} {:answer/id #uuid "14f50236-8fb1-578e-9ebf-1409fef9cf33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651080} {:answer/id #uuid "474bef80-4269-5543-aeea-683600c23e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651166} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4844c9-e2de-5c40-bb28-6454ae31f662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651317} {:answer/id #uuid "d15496e7-0084-5814-a2f9-3dc0711ae045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "474bef80-4269-5543-aeea-683600c23e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651166} :answer-field/id #uuid "36f96ef6-c7c5-5ca3-9f65-0a2be5e0b7a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3b84274-1d27-5bbc-b6e3-e108f3e1e00a" :question/math-academy-id "q-112201" :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\underbrace{(\\,3\\,)}_{{x}_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\underbrace{(\\,4\\,)}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
